.TH geectl-config-show 1  "geectl-config-show 0.2.4" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-config\-show \- Show the effective config: endpoint URLs with their source, and credential status (never a secret value)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl config show\fR [\fB\-\-resolve\-identity\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the effective config: endpoint URLs with their source, and credential status (never a secret value)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-resolve\-identity\fR
Resolve the OBS identity over the network too, like `changelog generate` does. Without it, `config show` reports the local levels and `obs (unresolved)` when the OBS account might still identify the author
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH VERSION
v0.2.4
